  "goodToKnow": "Die Ruine is a ruin: eine Burgruine (castle ruin), and Germany has thousands, especially along the Rhine. In 1945 many German cities lay in Ruinen; the Trümmerfrauen (rubble women) helped clear them. Berlin's Kaiser-Wilhelm-Gedächtniskirche was left as a ruin as a war memorial. The GDR anthem began Auferstanden aus Ruinen. Three syllables: ru-EE-ne. Ruinieren means to ruin. Plural: die Ruinen."
